5.text:
On the $w$ time scale the traces can be replaced by their stationary
means

\begin{equation*}
\langle v_{k}\rangle =\phi \mu_{k},\qquad 
\langle u_{k}\rangle =w\mu S_{k}, \qquad 
S_{k}\equiv\sum_{l}s_{kl},
\end{equation*}
and, up to the $k_{v}k_{u}$ overlap which can be absorbed in the
renormalised $\phi$,

\begin{equation*}
\langle u_{k}v_{k}\rangle
 =\phi w\mu^{2}\sum_{l}s_{kl}\bigl[1+c_{kl}\bigr],\qquad 
\langle x_{k}x_{l}\rangle=\mu_{k}\mu_{l}\bigl[1+c_{kl}\bigr],
\;c_{kk}=1 .
\end{equation*}
Hence on the $w$ scale

\begin{equation*}
0=\Big\langle\dot w_{k}\Big\rangle
\propto\langle u_{k}v_{k}\rangle+\rho\langle u_{k}\rangle ,
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
\phi\mu\sum_{l}s_{kl}\bigl[1+c_{kl}\bigr]+\rho S_{k}=0 .
\end{equation*}
With the homogeneous ansatz $w_{l}=w$, $\mu_{l}=\mu$, $c_{kl}=c$ for
$k\ne l$, $c_{kk}=1$, $s_{kk}=1$,

\begin{equation*}
\sum_{l}s_{kl}\bigl[1+c_{kl}\bigr]
 =S_{k}+1+c\,(S_{k}-1),
\end{equation*}
so that with the $k$ independent $S_{k}\equiv S$

\begin{equation*}
0=\phi\mu\Big[\,S+1+c\,(S-1)\Big]+\rho S ,
\end{equation*}
i.e.

\begin{equation*}
\frac{1+c\,(S-1)}{S}= -\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}\;,
\qquad 
c(S-1)=-\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}S-1 .
\end{equation*}
Writing the zero mean drift point as

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}= \frac{\kappa S-1}{S-1},\qquad c^{*}(S-1)=\kappa S-1 ,
\end{equation*}
the zero drift condition is $c^{*}(S-1)=\kappa_{\rm txt}S-1$ with on the
sign convention $\tau_{w}\dot w_{k}=u_{k}(v_{k}+\rho)$ used in the
statement

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{\rm txt}= -\,\frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}
              =-1-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu},
\end{equation*}
so that

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}= \frac{\kappa_{\rm txt}S-1}{S-1},\qquad 
0=\phi\mu\Big[\,S+1+c^{*}(S-1)\Big]+\rho S, 
\end{equation*}
and $|\kappa_{\rm txt}|=(\phi\mu+\rho)/\phi\mu$ is the dimensionless
local Hebbian gain.  Up to the inessential overall sign this is usually
written as the positive homeostatic gain

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{\rm eff}= \frac{\phi\mu+\rho}{\phi\mu}=1+\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu},
\qquad \phi\mu\,c_{\rm eff}(S)+\rho=0,
\end{equation*}
the ratio of the effective drive $\phi\mu+\rho$ to the bare drive
