correlation $c_{kk}=1$ can be absorbed in the definition of $S$ and the
positive number normally quoted in the dendritic clustering literature is

\begin{equation*}
\kappa_{0}= -\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}= \frac{\rho_{0}}{\phi\mu}>0,
\qquad 
\kappa_{\rm eff}=1-\kappa_{0},
\end{equation*}
so that, with the self term absorbed,

\begin{equation*}
c^{*}= \frac{\kappa_{0}S-1}{S-1},\qquad 
c_{\infty}=\lim_{S\to\infty}c^{*}= \kappa_{0}
          =-\frac{\rho}{\phi\mu}\;,
\end{equation*}
the familiar LTD/LTP ratio $\rho_{0}/\phi\mu$.
In the exact sign convention of the statement this is
$\kappa_{\rm txt}=-1-\rho/\phi\mu$, i.e. $|\kappa_{\rm txt}|=
1+\rho/\phi\mu$, which is the $-\rho/\phi\mu$ LTD/LTP ratio quoted up to
the $+1$ self-correlation shift.  The $\tau_{v},\tau_{u}$ filter overlap
is absorbed in the renormalised $\phi$ and does not appear
independently in the zero-crossing. ∎

